WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:10.603
Stay is a voice companion for adults with ADHD. It helps you start the thing you have been avoiding, and it does not talk over your pauses.

2
00:00:11.746 --> 00:00:23.170
Type or say what is in the way, and the dots become it. Overwhelmed is a tangle. Stuck is a staircase with one dot on the first step. Taxes are a coin.

3
00:00:25.106 --> 00:00:34.898
In the app you just talk. This is a simulated person, so you can see exactly what happens. Replies start about a second after you stop.

4
00:00:40.405 --> 00:00:47.437
People with ADHD pause mid-thought. Most voice assistants jump in. Stay waits.

5
00:01:19.664 --> 00:01:28.016
Parked, in one second. It can also start timers, run routines, set check-ins and keep a list for today.

6
00:01:30.995 --> 00:01:41.291
Everything on your mind, in any order. Stay picks one thing to start, a few for today, and the rest for later. No overdue, no guilt.

7
00:01:45.481 --> 00:01:54.601
Routines give you one visible next step, each with its own timer. Check-ins nudge you softly, even when the tab is in the background.

8
00:02:06.279 --> 00:02:27.663
We measured it with a simulated speaker. Replies in about 1.3 seconds, against 2.8 for the managed voice we replaced. It waited through the pause, noticed an interruption in well under a second, and never answered its own voice. We have not measured ChatGPT or Gemini, so we claim nothing against them.

9
00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:34.108
Stay. Open source, local-first, and built on AssemblyAI.
